    "report_markdown": "# Hypora run report: run_37363e5c028c\n\n**Outcome:** a verified model.\n\n## Task\n- Objective: Predict whether a credit applicant is a good or a bad customer.\n- Target: `good_or_bad_customer` (binary_classification)\n- Primary metric: `roc_auc` (maximize)\n\n## Summary\nThe run aimed to predict whether a credit applicant is a good or bad customer. It compared logistic regression and boosting approaches, then delivered a verified, regularized logistic regression model using one-hot encoded features.\n\n**Observations**\n- The final model's mean validation ROC-AUC was 0.7800.\n- Its test-split ROC-AUC was 0.7534.\n- Test-split recall was 0.8762.\n\n**Limitations**\n- The test split was scored once, so these results do not establish performance on other populations or future applicants.\n- No leakage candidates were flagged among the screened features, but that does not prove leakage is absent.\n- The learned-transform leakage check was skipped.\n\n_Written by the Reporter; every number above is filled in from stored metrics._\n\n## Final model\n- Trial `trl_b7719bd9`: Stronger shrinkage in the one-hot logistic model may reduce variance from sparse categorical levels and improve ROC-AUC on the limited credit sample.\n- Verified: yes\n\n| Metric | Test (once) | Validation (mean) |\n|---|---|---|\n| roc_auc | 0.7534 | 0.7800 |\n| accuracy | 0.7600 | 0.7467 |\n| balanced_accuracy | 0.6825 | 0.6540 |\n| precision | 0.8000 | 0.7817 |\n| recall | 0.8762 | 0.8857 |\n| f1 | 0.8364 | 0.8304 |\n| precision_macro | 0.7143 | 0.6967 |\n| recall_macro | 0.6825 | 0.6540 |\n| f1_macro | 0.6932 | 0.6649 |\n| pr_auc | 0.8663 | 0.8919 |\n| log_loss | 0.5315 | 0.5057 |\n| brier_score | 0.1749 | 0.1687 |\n\n| Check | Status | Detail |\n|---|---|---|\n| allowed_features | passed | trial code received exactly the contract's allowed features |\n| split_respected | passed | stratified split: disjoint, complete |\n| test_labels_not_accessed | passed | every predict stage saw features and the model only |\n| output_shape | passed | one prediction per planned row, task-shaped columns |\n| finite_outputs | passed | all predictions finite and well-formed |\n| metric_recomputation | passed | recomputed metrics match the harness |\n| artifact_loads | passed | the frozen model loaded in a sandbox and predicted the test split |\n| resource_limits | passed | every stage completed inside the submitted job's limits |\n| learned_transform_leakage | skipped | static analysis of fit/predict arrives with verifier v2 (S3.C4) |\n\n## Trials\n| Trial | Kind | Status | Validation roc_auc (mean \u00b1 std, folds) | Hypothesis |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `trl_3015ca66` | candidate | validated | 0.7745 \u00b1 0.0186 (3) | Shallow histogram gradient boosting can capture nonlinear interactions among credit attributes and improve ranking over the linear baseline. |\n| `trl_b7719bd9` | candidate | verified | 0.7800 \u00b1 0.0248 (3) | Stronger shrinkage in the one-hot logistic model may reduce variance from sparse categorical levels and improve ROC-AUC on the limited credit sample. |\n| `trl_cf7077b5` | candidate | validated | 0.7705 \u00b1 0.0206 (3) | A regularized stage-wise gradient boosting model on one-hot encoded attributes can rank credit risk better than logistic regression and histogram boosting on this small dataset. |\n| `trl_d3523c31` | baseline | validated | 0.7732 \u00b1 0.0286 (3) | A regularized logistic regression on scaled numeric and one-hot categorical features provides a robust linear baseline for credit risk. |\n\n## Data\n- Split: stratified, 20% test, stratified_kfold_3\n- Features used: 20; excluded: none\n- Leakage screen: No leakage candidates flagged among 20 screened features; this does not prove that leakage is absent.\n\n## Decision and faults\n- Decision: train (approved_plan)\n- Fault TOOL_UNAVAILABLE at submit_experiment: recovered\n\n## Run notes\n- Stage-1 placeholder (D-019): contract built by code, plan approved by policy; replaced by the Data Lead (S3.A2) and the plan gate (S3.D2).\n- The agent finished after 20 model turns, 18 tool calls; it nominated trl_b7719bd9.\n- Final candidate trl_b7719bd9: nominated by the agent.\n- Final job job_1794153324283473083_31dcb3: test split scored once; verifier v1 passed.\n\n## Sources\n- `task_spec:run_37363e5c028c.v1`\n- `profile:run_37363e5c028c.profile.af9994e073a8`\n- `experiment_contract:run_37363e5c028c.v1`\n- `result:trl_b7719bd9/test`\n"
